  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1257 PM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nCoastal trough moving in over Deep South Texas this afternoon with\nmost associated shower activity south of our forecast area. Have\nlimited PoPs for the afternoon to 20% mainly south and southwest.\nNot expecting much more than drizzle or some light showers.\nSurface winds are shifting back to the east and will eventually be\nsoutheast over the next couple of days which will keep the\nelevated low level moisture, though some slightly drier air may\ndrift into our northern areas behind a weak boundary briefly \ntomorrow afternoon.\n\nRain chances will be pretty minimal through the weekend though\na weak shortwave on Saturday will warrant a low (20%) chance for a\nfew showers. PWAT values are not impressive (only around 1-1.25\",\nso not expecting much. By early next week We'll see a shift in \nthe mid/upper level pattern with ridging shifting off to the east \nas a low pressure center moves into the center of the country. \nThis will bring another front near the area, but a consensus of \nguidance at this time suggests it doesn't have the strength to \npush all the way through - at least not with enough strength to \nreally notice it. We will have a medium chance for showers and \nstorms Tuesday into Wednesday through. \n\nOverall temperatures are expected to be fairly seasonal in terms\nof highs and a bit above normal for lows.",
